title: A vote of no confidence is called against the current government!
subtitle: We have angered our coalition partners too much...
new-page: true
view-if: dvp_in_government and (coalition_dissent > 3 and in_weimar_coalition) or (coalition_dissent > 2 and in_weimar_coalition == 0) and dvp_r < 50 and not constructive_vonc
tags: event
go-to: vonc_menu

# Options: spend relations to reduce coalition_dissent

= Vote of No Confidence

[? if spd_in_government: The SPD ?][? if spd_in_government == 0 and z_in_government: The Center Party ?][? if z_in_government == 0 and dnvp_in_government: The Center Party ?] has called for a vote of no confidence against us, due to our various policies and disagreements. If this succeeds, there will be an election in a few months.

@vonc_menu

- @try_assuage: Try to assuage our partners.
- @let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.

@try_assuage

How do we assuage our partners?

- @concessions: Make broad concessions to our coalition partners.
- @resources: Use our resources to reduce dissent within the coalition.
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@concessions
view-if: not secularized
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 0; workers_dvp -= 10; new_middle_dvp -= 15; old_middle_dvp -= 15; rural_dvp -= 10; liberal_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; industrialist_dissent += 10; nationalist_dissent += 15;

We yield in several policy areas to maintain the stability of our coalition. The vote has been called off.

@resources
view-if: secularized = 0
choose-if: resources >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough resources.
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1;

By transferring resources to our coalition partners, we can reduce their dissent against our policies. This is a crude, but effective solution.

@let_it_happen
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 0; foreign_minister_party = dvp_name; finance_minister_party = dvp_name; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = dvp_name; finance_minister_party = "DVP"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Stegerwald"; interior_minister = "Wirth"; finance_minister = "Moldenhauer"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; foreign_minister = "Stresemann"; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener";  coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; workers_spd -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; old_middle_nsdap += 4 if pro_republic < 50; new_middle_nsdap += 3 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: let_it_happen_hindenburg if president != "Braun"; let_it_happen_braun if president == "Braun"

@let_it_happen_hindenburg
on-arrival: chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; welfare -= 2;

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Brüning has been appointed as the head of an acting government, consisting solely of the bourgeois parties. He immediately proceeds to cut welfare spending substantially.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@let_it_happen_braun
on-arrival: spd_caretaker = 1

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] remains as the head of a caretaker government, but no longer has the power to enact new policies.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
